      "caveat": "IMPORTANT — the wording needs changing on two counts. (1) Place: the Commons geotag is 43.45798, 42.99347, which I make 8.4 km NW of the Aktoprak pass (43.4083, 43.0722), in the Bylym / Gizhgit basin at the Baksan end of the Aktoprak road. It is the same clay-hill country the road runs through and it is inside this trip, but it is NOT the pass. Caption it as e.g. 'The bare clay hills above Bylym, at the foot of the Aktoprak road' — do not write 'the Aktoprak pass'. (2) Colour: 'fired-clay coloured' overstates it. The mid-ground hills are ochre-to-khaki with rust-brown strata rather than red; roughly a third of the frame (upper slopes, foreground shrub) is muted green. 'Striated, treeless, ochre eroded hillsides' is accurate; 'red-brown' is not. Also note the Gizhgit reservoir appears small in this frame, so it will read as a wide establishing shot of the same lake that aktoprak-02 shows close up — deliberate sequencing, but worth knowing. Licence is CC BY-SA 3.0: attribution required and any cropped derivative must itself be released share-alike.",
